~ vorkoth_transformation_intro
vorkoth_p1: *laughing* You actually landed a few. I'll admit... didn't expect that.

vorkoth_p1: Guess I'll stop holding back, then.
=> END

~ vorkoth_transformation_reveal
npcgreen: It's... it's true, then. He really is one of them.

npcblue: All this time...

vorkoth_p2: THIS is what it takes to lead. THIS is what real strength looks like. Not whatever it is you four think you're doing.

astryn: ...Right. Guess we do this the hard way.
=> END

~ vorkoth_defeat
vorkoth_p1: ...heh. Didn't think you had it in you.

astryn: Give it up. Step down. Give back what you've stolen from this city, and maybe... maybe... these people find it in them to forgive you.

vorkoth_p1: Forgive me. For what? Running this city the only way it's ever worked?

vorkoth_p1: I'd do it again. Every coin, every tariff, every debt I called in. This city breathes because I make it breathe. Take that away and watch how fast it starves without me.

novius: You know how many times I said no to people who couldn't pay? Watched their faces when I did it, telling myself it wasn't my fault, that it was just how things worked. I still see that look on this whole city every time you open your mouth.

vorkoth_p1: Then you understand. Someone has to make the hard calls. I just made mine honestly. I didn't dress it up as kindness like you did.

astryn: That's not power. That's just theft with a title.

vorkoth_p1: Call it whatever lets you sleep at night. I built something here. You just want to burn it down and call it justice.

vorkoth_p1: Go on, then. Everyone's watching. Let's see what you really are underneath all that talk.
=> END

# Astryn's walk-over and draw (a pistol from a holster strapped to her thigh, a weapon she
# never uses in battle) plays out in code between here and the line below; see
# BossTurnBasedCombat._play_vorkoth_ending_sequence().
~ vorkoth_defeat_confrontation
vorkoth_p1: ...That's not your style.

astryn: Special occasion, asshole.

- Spare Vorkoth => vorkoth_spare_check
- Kill Vorkoth => vorkoth_kill

# Routes to the Novius-intervenes version of sparing him if Astryn and Novius bonded
# earlier (dialogue_novius.dialogue's ~ full_conversation_2 node), otherwise the normal
# (fatal) spare outcome.
~ vorkoth_spare_check
if QuestManager.novius_bonded == true:
	=> vorkoth_spare_novius_intervenes
=> vorkoth_spare

~ vorkoth_kill
do QuestManager.vorkoth_ending = "kill"

astryn: ...For justice.
# Cut to black.
=> END

~ vorkoth_spare_novius_intervenes
do QuestManager.vorkoth_ending = "spare_novius_intervened"

astryn: ...No. You're not worth it.
=> END

# Astryn's walk back to the team, and Novius's stab beat with Vorkoth, play out in code
# between here and the title below; see BossTurnBasedCombat._play_vorkoth_ending_sequence().
~ vorkoth_spare_novius_mercy_taunt
vorkoth_p1: ...Mercy. From you.
=> END

~ vorkoth_spare_novius_aftermath
astryn: ...Nov.

novius: I told you. I know exactly what he costs people.

astryn: ...Thank you.

novius: Don't spare men like him again.
=> END

~ vorkoth_spare
do QuestManager.vorkoth_ending = "spare_fail"

astryn: ...No. You're not worth it.
=> END

# Astryn's holster-and-idle blink, the walk away, Vorkoth's teleport strike, the cut to
# black, and the final wait all play out in code between here and the title below; see
# BossTurnBasedCombat._play_vorkoth_ending_sequence().
~ vorkoth_spare_mercy_taunt
vorkoth_p1: ...Mercy. From you.
=> END

~ vorkoth_spare_aftermath
vorkoth_p1: YOU SEE?! You see what happens to those who think they can challenge me?!

vorkoth_p1: Levaris does not bow to radicals! Let this "Justice" nonsense die with her!
=> END

~ duel_intro
paanouncer: Ladies and gentlemen of Levaris! Tonight, in accordance with the challenge issued at this morning's podium, we bring you a duel for the ages!

paanouncer: In this corner: the undisputed, unbroken defender of this city, the People's General himself... VORKOTH!

*The crowd cheers, though a little too on cue, a little too rehearsed.*

paanouncer: And challenging him tonight... representing themselves as...

paanouncer: ..."The Merciless Blades of Absolute Justice"?

astryn: The what.

novius: Please tell me that's a joke.

aegrandir: ...Spero.

spero: One of the guards asked me what to call us for the announcement. Someone had to answer.

astryn: And you said THAT.

spero: In my defense, "The Justice Bros" was my second choice.

novius: That's WORSE.

vorkoth_p1: The Merciless Blades of Absolute Justice! Wonderful. Truly. I almost don't want to embarrass you.

astryn: I'm breaking your jaw after this, Spero.

spero: Noted. After we win.
=> END
